.TH BUNNYDNS 1 "2026-08-31" "bunnydns 0.7.0" "SCS Commands"
.SH NAME
bunnydns \- inspect, edit, and reconcile Bunny DNS records
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bunnydns
.br
.B bunnydns
.BR help | version
.br
.B bunnydns init-key
.I keyfile
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.B list
.I zone
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.B list --records-file
.I records.json
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.B add
.I zone type name value
.RI [ record-options ]
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.B update
.I zone record-id record-options
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.B delete
.I zone record-id
.br
.B bunnydns
.RI [ global-options ]
.BR validate | check | plan | apply | verify | prune
.I records.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bunnydns
edits individual records or reconciles project-owned records from a JSON file.
It operates on an existing Bunny DNS zone and preserves unrelated records.
.PP
With no arguments, it prints version and usage, exits successfully, and
changes nothing.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Global options must appear before the command.
.TP
.BI --api-key " file"
Use this absolute protected key-file path.
Direct commands default to
.IR $HOME/.secrets/bunnynet-api-key .
.TP
.BI --backup-dir " directory"
Use this absolute pre-change snapshot directory.
Direct changes default to
.IR $HOME/.local/state/bunnydns/backups .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Print usage.
.TP
.B version
Print the release version.
.TP
.BI init-key " keyfile"
Prompt through the controlling terminal and create a new mode-0600 key file.
An existing file is never overwritten.
.TP
.BI validate " records.json"
Validate local JSON without reading the key or using the network.
.TP
.BI check " records.json"
Validate dependencies, key protection, API access, owner, and exact zone
lookup.  This command is read-only.
.TP
.BI list " zone"
Print every record and numeric record ID.  This command is read-only.
.TP
.BI "list --records-file" " records.json"
Read the zone and key-file path from the JSON file, then list every zone
record.  This command is read-only.
.TP
.BI add " zone type name value " "[record-options]"
Write a snapshot, create one record, fetch the zone, and verify the submitted
fields.
.TP
.BI update " zone record-id record-options"
Write a snapshot and change only the named fields.  A name or type change uses
delete-then-create and may assign a new record ID.
.TP
.BI delete " zone record-id"
Write a snapshot, delete the exact numeric ID, verify its absence, and print
the deleted record.
.TP
.BI plan " records.json"
Print OK, CREATE, UPDATE, REPLACE, or CONFLICT for each declared record.
This command is read-only.
.TP
.BI apply " records.json"
Back up the zone, apply a conflict-free plan, fetch the zone, and require a
clean verified plan.
.TP
.BI verify " records.json"
Require every declared record to match.  This command is read-only.
.TP
.BI prune " records.json"
After verification, delete only obsolete records owned by this declaration.
.SH RECORD OPTIONS
.B add
accepts
.BR --ttl ,
.BR --priority ,
.BR --weight ,
.BR --port ,
.BR --flags ,
.BR --tag ,
.BR --disable ,
and
.BR --enable .
.PP
.B update
also accepts
.BR --type ,
.BR --name ,
and
.BR --value .
Use
.B @
for the zone apex.
TTL defaults to 60; numeric routing fields default to zero.
.PP
Supported types are A, AAAA, CNAME, TXT, MX, SRV, CAA, PTR, NS, SVCB,
HTTPS, and TLSA.
.SH RECORDS FILE
The top-level JSON object contains:
.TP
.B owner
Stable lowercase project namespace, up to 64 characters.
.TP
.B zone
Existing Bunny DNS zone name.
.TP
.B key_file
Absolute protected API key-file path.
.TP
.B backup_dir
Absolute pre-change snapshot directory.
.TP
.B records
Desired record array.  An empty array is valid.
.PP
Each record requires a unique lowercase
.BR key ,
.BR type ,
.BR name ,
and non-empty
.BR value .
Optional fields are
.BR ttl ,
.BR priority ,
.BR weight ,
.BR port ,
.BR flags ,
.BR tag ,
.BR disabled ,
and
.BR allow_multiple .
.SH OWNERSHIP
Declarative records use this Bunny comment:
.PP
.RS
managed-by:OWNER; key=KEY
.RE
.PP
The owner isolates projects sharing a zone.  The key identifies a record
across value and TTL changes.  Duplicate ownership comments, ambiguous
unmanaged matches, and CNAME conflicts stop the plan.
.PP
.B prune
only deletes records with this declaration's owner prefix.  Do not run another
writer against the same zone during
.B apply
or
.BR prune .
.SH API KEY
The key file must be regular, non-symbolic, mode 0400 or 0600, and contain
exactly one printable ASCII line without leading or trailing spaces.
The secret is not placed in an environment variable or process argument.
Only the key-file path is passed to the internal Node helper.
.SH BACKUPS
Before add, update, delete, apply, or prune, the current zone document is saved
to a mode-0600 file in a mode-0700 directory.  Changes are sequential and are
not rolled back automatically; retain the snapshot for recovery.
.SH INSTALLATION
Prepare dependencies and install:
.PP
.RS
npm ci --ignore-scripts
.br
gmake install
.RE
.PP
On macOS the command is installed under
.IR $HOME/bin ,
the runtime under
.IR $HOME/libexec/bunnydns ,
and the manual under
.IR $HOME/share/man/man1 .
.PP
SmartOS global-zone defaults are below
.IR /opt/custom .
SmartOS native-zone defaults are below
.IR /opt/local .
Use
.B gmake
on SmartOS.
.PP
.B gmake update
compares fresh MD5 digests and the installed runtime.  Identical content is
left untouched; differing content is uninstalled and installed sequentially.
Absolute BINDIR, LIBEXECDIR, MANDIR, and DESTDIR overrides are supported.
.SH PORTABILITY
Requires POSIX shell utilities, jq 1.6 or newer, Node.js 18 or newer, npm, and
Bunny's pinned official OpenAPI client.  GNU Make and an MD5 tool are required
for project checks and installation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.secrets/bunnynet-api-key
Default direct-command key file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.local/state/bunnydns/backups
Default direct-command snapshot directory.
.TP
.I records.example.json
Copyable declarative schema example.
.TP
.I bunnydns.md5
Source-tree command checksum sidecar.
.TP
.I bunnydns-node.mjs.md5
Source-tree helper checksum sidecar.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage, validation, dependency, permission, API, conflict, or verification
failure.
.TP
.B 130
Handled HUP, INT, or TERM signal.
